<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Version>0.16.0</Version>
		<Authors>Codeer</Authors>
		<Company>Codeer</Company>
		<Description>Extra field components and client-side services for Codeer.LowCode.Blazor. Includes Calendar, Gantt Chart, Task Board (Kanban), Rich Text Editor, Markdown Editor, Color Picker, Marker List, QR Code, Progress Bar, Password Hash, and AI Text Analyzer fields, plus built-in script objects (Excel, WebApi, Toaster, Mail) and client infrastructure services (HTTP, UI, logging, localization).</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Codeer-Software/Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Codeer-Software/Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>Blazor;LowCode;Codeer;Calendar;Gantt;Kanban;TaskBoard;RichText;Markdown;ColorPicker;QRCode;Progress;PasswordHash</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>New: EditHistoryField and EditHistoryContractField (edit history). Put EditHistoryField on a module and every save of a record of that module (create, update, delete) is recorded in a history module as a snapshot of the whole record including its owned records (detail rows, Gantt tasks and the like) (the recording is done by EditHistoryRecorder in Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server 0.15.0, wired in the app templates). On the detail page the field lists the versions (number, change type, user, date and only the changed fields as old -&gt; new; list rows as added / removed / changed), shows a past version in a view-only dialog with the changed fields highlighted, and restores a version by applying it to the form: the user saves to confirm, so permissions, validation, optimistic locking and the history of the restore itself all go through the normal save. The history module declares its field names with EditHistoryContractField (roles ModuleName / DataId / ChangeType / Snapshot required, UserId / DateTime optional; design checks for missing fields, wrong types and duplicates; the roles follow renames). EditHistoryChangeType (Add / Update / Delete) is a design enum. History is read through the normal module data API, so who can see it is the read permission of the history module. Version numbers are not stored but numbered from the count at display time. Not covered: restoring attached files (only name and key are recorded). Also new: EditHistoryUndeleteButtonField, placed on the history module, restores a deleted record: for a module with logical delete the record and its owned records come back with their Ids (links keep working; recorded as a Restore version), for a module with physical delete a new record is created from the snapshot. Restoring a version also revives logically deleted list rows with their Ids (the undelete is sent with the save and confirmed in the same transaction). The version list shows only "record created" for a create, collapses list rows behind their summary, and shows just "changed" for field types that cannot be rendered as text. Edit history cannot be combined with the delete archive (design check). The records of a version are the record itself plus the owned records declared with IOwnedRecordsFieldDesign of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 (a list declares its rows when they belong to the record; GanttFieldDesign, CalendarFieldDesign, TaskBoardFieldDesign and MarkerListFieldDesign now declare their child records, so they are recorded without an extra list; GanttFieldDesign also declares its dependencies as "&lt;field&gt;:Dependencies", so the arrows are recorded, listed in the diff, shown in the version dialog and restored, with the task references of recreated tasks re-pointed to the new rows). A field that implements IOwnedRecordsField of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 (GanttField, CalendarField, TaskBoardField and MarkerListField do) also takes part in "restore this version" and "show this version"; the interface lives in the framework, so an extension field can take part without referencing this package. To open the record a history row belongs to, put an AnchorTagField of the framework on the history module with ModuleVariable = ModuleName.Value and IdVariable = DataId.Value (the setup generates it as OpenTarget). In the version dialog the owned records shown by GanttField, CalendarField, TaskBoardField and MarkerListField are now highlighted per item (added / changed / removed, the removed ones taken from the previous version), and Gantt and Calendar move to the first highlighted item when none is in view; the rows are passed to IOwnedRecordsField.ShowOwnedRecordsAsync as OwnedRecordRow of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 with the CSS classes to apply, and the list rows of the record go through the same interface (ListField implements it). "Restore this version" tells the user when nothing of the version could be applied to the form. Works with AutoSubmitField: the version list is reloaded after every auto save (an auto save does not reload the record, so the list stayed stale). Works with ApprovalFlowField on the same module: the approval flow key, which the approval API writes after the save, is left out of the version diff and is not touched by "restore this version" (submit and resubmit are recorded as versions of the applicant; approve, reject and return are recorded in the approval history only). Fixed: ApprovalFlowField now reloads the record after a submit or resubmit of an already saved record (the navigation to the same URL was a no-op, so the field kept showing "not submitted" and the edit lock did not take effect until the page was reloaded). Embedded modules (ModuleField) are part of the record: ModuleFieldDesign of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 declares its child record as an owned record and ModuleField implements IOwnedRecordsField, so the child is recorded with the version, its changed fields are listed like the rows of a list, the version dialog highlights them inside the child module, and "restore this version" applies the child's fields (and the parent's reference to it) so the child is saved with the parent. The change date of a version follows SaveAsUtc of the DateTime field of the history module. Design check: owned records that are not held in full at runtime (OwnedRecordsDesign.HoldsAllRecords of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 is false, for example a detail list with server-side paging) are reported on the module with EditHistoryField, including nested owned records, because "restore this version" replaces the whole set; use in-memory paging or no row limit for such lists. EditHistoryField can now name owned records (by declaration name, nested as "Items.Details") that are left out of the history entirely (ExcludedOwnedRecords: not recorded, not in the diff, the dialog or a restore) or recorded per row (IndividuallyRecordedOwnedRecords: the rows saved with the parent are recorded in the row module's own history, one version per row, and are not part of the parent's version; the row module needs its own EditHistoryField, checked at design time). Versions recorded before such a setting are read as if the records were not there (a path in both settings is design check EditHistoryFieldDesign:7). The paths and the LayoutName follow renames. The diff and the field highlight of the version dialog compare the full text (not the 300 characters shown), the change date and DateTime values saved as UTC are shown in local time, and the read permission of the fields of detail rows is taken from the row module. The history module created by the setup gets an index on (module_name, data_id) and, on SQL Server and Oracle, sized columns for it. Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageId>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras</PackageId>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup>
		<StaticWebAssetFingerprintingEnabled>false</StaticWebAssetFingerprintingEnabled>
		<StaticWebAssetsFingerprintContent>false</StaticWebAssetsFingerprintContent>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- internal はファミリー内(Server/Designer)とテストにだけ見せる (ファミリー外の製品アセンブリへのIVTは不可) -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Designer</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Test</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Codeer.LowCode.Blazor" Version="1.3.37" />
		<PackageReference Include="Markdig" Version="0.37.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="QRCoder" Version="1.7.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities" Version="8.0.8" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="8.0.8" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="8.0.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Excel.Report.PDF" Version="0.36.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Sotsera.Blazor.Toaster" Version="3.0.0" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<EmbeddedResource Update="Properties\Resources.resx">
			<Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
			<LastGenOutput>Resources.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
		</EmbeddedResource>
		<EmbeddedResource Update="Properties\Resources.ja-JP.resx">
			<Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
			<LastGenOutput>Resources.ja-JP.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
		</EmbeddedResource>
		<Compile Update="Properties\Resources.Designer.cs">
			<DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
			<AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
			<DependentUpon>Resources.resx</DependentUpon>
		</Compile>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
